| cChrCmdBtnChrg | — | Embedded at cChrCmd+0x138; `reset` (0x140029050) zeroes only +0x14..+0x23 inline; ctor allocates nothing. | **CLEAR** (inline) |
| cChrCmdCombo | — | Same 0x218 B layout as base (operator_new 0x218); dtor → `FUN_140025430`, frees only `+0x178`. No extra heap. | **CLEAR** (inline) |
| cChrCmdLimit | — | Embedded at cChrCmd+0x8; `reset` (0x14002C1F0) writes ~0x118 B all inline; no allocation. | **CLEAR** (inline) |
| cChrCmd +0x168 | +0x168 | Command-list resource ptr (static .lot-style resource, set via allocAndResetLineBuffer arg) | CLEAR (stable resource, keep ptr) |
| cChrCmd +0x1E8 | +0x1E8 | 6 qwords zeroed in ctor, never freed in dtor → non-owning ptrs into command-list resource | CLEAR (stable resource) |
| cAtkCtrl | +80/+848/+1616 | 3× MtArray<cPlayDataAccumulate>[32] (0x18 B × 32 each) — **inline** within the 2384 B body (cChr+6264), covered by flat char save. Dtor destructs in place, no free. | **CLEAR** (inline) |
| cChrInput | +0x21C8 | `initInputBuffer` (0x14002E440) does inline memset/stores only, zero allocation; all rings embedded in 0x570 body. | **CLEAR** (inline) |
| mpChainSetup | cChr+0x67F0 | Points to sChainSetup static resource (per field map §3) | CLEAR (stable resource) |
| sReplay | +0x?? | Full replay input buffer (internal pointers, skip) | SKIPPED (stale ptrs) |
| uShot | +0x08 | Circular-list node linkage (not heap-array, captured by walk) | CAPTURED |
| cGameEffect | pool | Per-effect state nodes (pool allocator, skip) | SKIPPED |

**Audit conclusion (Ghidra, dtor-based ownership analysis):** the shared cChrCmd
teardown `FUN_140025430` — used by base, Spatk, and Combo dtors — frees exactly
one heap block: the `+0x178` line buffer. Both subclasses are the identical
0x218 B size as the base class (their `operator_new` calls request 0x218), so
they add vfn overrides only, no fields. BtnChrg (embedded at +0x138) and Limit
(embedded at +0x8) are fully inline. Therefore the `+0x178` fix covers ALL
cChrCmd-family heap state. cAtkCtrl's three cPlayDataAccumulate arrays are
inline per its ctor (`MtArray__initElements(this+80/+848/+1616, 0x18, 0x20, ...)`)
and land inside the flat character snapshot.

